Renderer configuration
----------------------
Real MuPDF PDF parsing and drawing, including text, vectors, multiple pages,
embedded images, compressed streams, embedded font formats, transparency,
ICC color and JPEG2000/JBIG2/JPEG decoding. Only the PDF document agent is
selected. PDF JavaScript is disabled; it is not part of passive rasterizing.
TOFU/TOFU_CJK retain standard PDF base14 fallback only. Droid CJK fallback
is not linked because its multi-megabyte payload exceeds the existing VIFS1
loader's staging heap. Non-embedded CJK font substitution is unavailable;
CJK and other scripts still render through document-embedded fonts. The large
Noto/SIL fallback collection is also not embedded. Password-protected documents
needing a password return an explicit error because the protocol has no
password field.
Brotli, HTML-rich annotation layout, OCR and export-to-office agents are off.
The upstream slim FreeType module/options configuration is used unchanged.

Service bounds: one live owner-TID-scoped handle, 2 MiB copied input, 1M page
pixels, 3072-byte pixel chunks, 10 MiB MuPDF allocator budget, 16 MiB cell heap.
The sole full raster allocation is a four-component RGB+alpha MuPDF pixmap
rendered onto opaque white. C closes/drops its draw device, checks packed
opaque RGBA, swaps R/B in-place, and retains the pixmap only as a BGRA byte
cache until the next render/Close. No full-page RGB/BGRA duplicate exists.
A new Open while occupied returns busy, even to another TID. Handles are never
recycled; exhaustion is explicit. Failed raster production clears the cache;
invalid argument rejection does not modify an existing cache. Close
drops cached BGRA, document/streams, context and allocator, then Rust input.
No mmap, domain/shared-memory grant, SpawnCap or self-registration is used.
Clock-dependent C time() returns the standard unavailable sentinel (-1);
parsing and formatting timestamps already present in PDFs uses real UTC
calendar conversion. No wall-clock epoch is invented.

Freestanding ABI
----------------
Sole production target: riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf, RV64GC/lp64d, PIC/medany.
CC_riscv64gc_unknown_none_elf selects the compiler, otherwise
riscv-none-elf-gcc is selected. An unsupported target fails build.rs clearly.
No hosted libc or C++ runtime is linked. Compiler intrinsic headers provide
stddef/stdint/stdarg/float; owned vendor/include supplies the rest.
Source-derived external ABI requirements (not an observed nm inventory):
* api POSIX: malloc, calloc, realloc, free; memcpy/memmove/memset/memcmp/
  memchr; strlen/strcmp/strncmp/strcpy/strncpy/strcat/strchr/strrchr;
  fprintf/sprintf/snprintf/vsnprintf/vsprintf/vfprintf/fputs/fputc/fwrite,
  stdout/stderr; abort; double/float C99 math functions (libm-backed).
* Service-local C: prefixed qsort/bsearch, integer parsing, extra string
  operations, lrintf, errno, UTC calendar operations, absent environment;
  __popcountdi2 is implemented with exact 64-bit parallel bit summation in
  the same lp64d archive (avoids incompatible compiler_builtins objects).
  ocel_pdf_remove fails with EACCES/-1: this passive service never mutates
  files, including LCMS profile-writing cleanup reachable at static link.
* Service-local Rust: ocel_pdf_exit invokes the real cell exit syscall.
* Service-local assembly: ocel_pdf_setjmp/ocel_pdf_longjmp save ra/sp,
  s0..s11 and fs0..fs11 in 26 words. They do NOT use the shared api POSIX
  setjmp (which currently saves only fs0/fs1). All MuPDF exception frames
  and codec error boundaries stay in C; there are no throwing Rust callbacks.
IJG's documented NO_GETENV configuration disables JPEGMEM environment parsing
and its sscanf dependency; cells have no process environment to consult.
File, exporter and process-environment declarations needed to compile unused
upstream API sections are present, but these sections are removed by function/
data section GC. The service opens only ostd::fs::File bounded read buffers
and passes fz_open_memory; no MuPDF file-opening entry point is invoked.
The final RV64 link and nm undefined-symbol closure must be checked by parent;
no link or smoke execution was performed during this worker assignment.

Parent verification entry points
-------------------------------
1. From repository root:
   python3 cells/services/ocel-pdf/smoke/host.py tests/fixtures/ocel-pdf-demo.pdf
   This compiles the same pinned renderer/dependency selection against host
   libc and asserts C exception recovery, two real raster pages, opaque BGRA,
   text and colored vector pixels, cache/range rejection. It is a native C
   harness, NOT an unsupported-target service fallback.
2. Parent adds workspace member, then:
   cargo build -p ocel-pdf --release --target riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf
   Use the project's normal cross-compiler/linker environment. Inspect the
   service ELF with readelf/nm for unresolved symbols and section sizes; ELF
   plus font data plus 16MiB heap and stack must fit the existing 32MiB slot.
3. Parent image/QEMU smoke: init registers OCEL_PDF=18, Open the fixture,
   require pages=2, RenderPage(0/1,320,240), collect ReadPixels chunks, require
   each raster is 307200 bytes with alpha=255 and distinct colored/text/image
   content; Close. Also exercise invalid bytes through Open (C catch path),
   page/size/range/closed-handle errors, and a different sender TID's inability
   to render/read/close an owner's document. Test local RV64 exception recovery
   with live fs2..fs11 values across the prefixed setjmp/longjmp if possible.
